{#
_calendar_pane.html.twig — the calendar docked beside the mail panes.

The container, the handle and the sizing are _side_pane.html.twig's, shared
with the address book. What is the calendar's own is below.

Its ui--split lives on the row in _mailbox.html.twig, not here: it owns the
boundary between two panes and the switch's three positions, and its scope has
to reach the topbar's switch as well as this. So the wrapper is that
controller's `wrapper` target, which it shows and hides.

Below lg it is still this pane, not a different page — it just takes the whole
row and the mail steps aside (see [data-calendar-mode] in app.css). The row
cannot hold a sidebar, a usable list and a usable calendar at once under
1024px, so rather than squeezing both under their minimums the calendar takes
over. That is also what the switch's third position does at every width. Same
control, same DOM, no navigation: going back to the mail puts it back exactly
as it was.
#}

{% set paneOpen = app.user.isCalendarPaneOpen %}

{% embed '_partials/_side_pane.html.twig' with {
    name: 'calendar',
    open: paneOpen,
    widthVar: '--calendar-pane-width',
    handleLabel: 'calendar.pane.resize'|trans,
    attrs: 'data-ui--split-target="wrapper"',
} %}
    {% block side_pane_body %}
        {# A pane the user will see on first paint is rendered WITH the page —
           embedding the same controller the frame's src would have fetched —
           so a reload shows mail and calendar together instead of a spinner
           that fills in a beat later. The frame element is still the shell
           (week/view navigation inside it still swaps only the pane); it just
           starts full instead of lazy. A closed pane keeps the lazy empty
           frame: its src is set the first time the switch opens it, and
           nobody pays for a calendar they are not looking at. #}
        {% if open %}
            {{ render(controller('App\\Controller\\Calendar\\CalendarController::pane')) }}
        {% else %}
            <turbo-frame
                id="calendar-pane-frame"
                loading="lazy"
                class="flex flex-col min-h-0 flex-1"
            >
                <div class="flex items-center justify-center h-24 text-ink-faint" aria-live="polite">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </div>
            </turbo-frame>
        {% endif %}
    {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
